7] [17592186111031 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "9cb9b8d4-254b-58ff-bc4a-531da47e017a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111031 #edb/ref 1074 "First, let's recall the product rule for logarithms:\n\n$$\n{log}_{n}⁡a+{log}_{n}⁡b={log}_{n}⁡(ab)\n$$\n\nUsing the product rule for logarithms, we can combine the first two terms as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{log}_{5}⁡2+{log}_{5}⁡4+{log}_{5}⁡6 & ={log}_{5}⁡(2\\cdot 4)+{log}_{5}⁡6 \\\\  & ={log}_{5}⁡8+{log}_{5}⁡6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the product rule for logarithms once more, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{log}_{5}⁡8+{log}_{5}⁡6 & ={log}_{5}⁡(8\\cdot 6) \\\\  & ={log}_{5}⁡48.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111644 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186111645 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111644 #edb/ref 1061 455954 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111644 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "4804adec-ffac-52d5-9554-90532fefcf46" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111644 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186111877 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111645 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186111646 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111645 #edb/ref 1061 455955 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111645 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "da9135a3-0714-5821-9342-7af0dfdc24c1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111645 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186110696 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111646 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186111647 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111646 #edb/ref 1061 455958 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111646 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "70bdbc7f-5a0f-5a93-968c-2aea21b191b2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111646 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186110697 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111647 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186111648 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111647 #edb/ref 1061 455961 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111647 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "43bc1a3b-9e83-53c1-a693-6ff91e1f9a45" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111647 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186110698 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111648 #edb/ref 1061 455964 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111648 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "77cd3268-d65f-5cf1-8123-2cf48af729df" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111648 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186110699 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111877 #edb/ref 1064 "We can simplify the addition of two logarithms that share a base using the **product rule** for logarithms.\n\nThe **product rule** states that two logarithms which share a common base $\\color{blue}n$ satisfy\n\n$$\n\\log_{\\color{blue}n}(a) + \\log_{\\color{blue}n}(b) = \\log_{\\color{blue}n}\\left( ab\\right).\n$$\n\nSo, we can use the product rule to rewrite $\\log_{\\color{blue}5}(4) + \\log_{\\color{blue}5}(3)$ as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{log}_{5}⁡4+{log}_{5}⁡(3) & ={log}_{5}⁡(4\\cdot 3) \\\\  & ={log}_{5}⁡(12).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe product rule works exactly the same for the natural and common logarithms." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111877 #edb/ref 1065 2782 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111877 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "a915130a-f6b9-5fec-a625-3d6d987255ac" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111877 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186539480 #edb/ref 1080 "2+{log}_{4}⁡({x}^{3})" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186539480 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186539480 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "020e75fa-c086-57b4-9ebf-21542d8c63cc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186539482 #edb/ref 1080 "6{log}_{2}⁡({x}^{2})+{log}_{2}⁡y" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186539482 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186539482 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "03195d80-906e-5fc4-b665-ca11a907a266" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186539488 #edb/ref 1080 "t^6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186539488 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186539488 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "04eea80b-51f5-55aa-bacb-612eb84f806e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186539505 #edb/ref 1080 "64\\operatorname{log}⁡64" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186539505 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 1759218